          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "retune-semantic-zoom-thresholds"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Sketch, Not Confirmed\n\nThis graph is my first-pass reasoning from one line Michael gave during a live review — \"detail should be much closer to 3... we aren’t spending enough time at icon size\" — grounded in the actual current constants (WORKSPACE_PRESENTATION_THRESHOLDS in graphWorkspace.js), not a validated design.\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Is this universal, or specific to rich web-authored content? (see the open Question node)\n- Should this be a retune of the existing shared constants, or a move to content-aware thresholds? (see the Alternative node)\n- What are the actual target numbers? None are proposed here yet — that needs the comparison in the Next Step before picking values."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "portId": "guided-by",
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
