        "action": "Before changing the shared constants, record where a few different graphs (one dense with authored web views, one plain/node-heavy) currently cross each threshold while zooming, side by side, to see whether one retuned scale actually serves both — or whether the content-aware alternative is the real answer.",
        "expectedEvidence": "Screenshots or logged occupancy values at each transition, for at least two visibly different content types, showing whether their ideal thresholds actually diverge.",
        "status": "open",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "retune-semantic-zoom-thresholds"
        },
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "ArrowForward"
          }
